From: Takoserver Native source candidate
Subject: [SOURCE ONLY v6.12] refuse owned batch-verdict metadata edits

Against v6.12 with the retained tako_terminal base and NFQUEUE pieces.
Checks each actual extracted entry before mark/priority mutation.
Uses existing DROP cleanup and continues the original safe batch iterator.
Config-off/unowned behavior stays unchanged. No terminal/grant or build claim.

diff --git a/net/netfilter/nfnetlink_queue.c b/net/netfilter/nfnetlink_queue.c
--- a/net/netfilter/nfnetlink_queue.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nfnetlink_queue.c
@@ -1334,6 +1334,12 @@
 		return -ENOENT;
 
 	list_for_each_entry_safe(entry, tmp, &batch_list, list) {
+		/* Refuse this real entry before batch packet metadata edits. */
+		if (unlikely(tako_terminal_block(entry->state.net, entry->state.pf))) {
+			nfqnl_reinject(entry, NF_DROP);
+			continue;
+		}
+
 		if (nfqa[NFQA_MARK])
 			entry->skb->mark = ntohl(nla_get_be32(nfqa[NFQA_MARK]));
 
